      "n": 1,
      "signpost": "one or the other",
      "definition": "used before a singular noun, when there are two possibilities, to mean one or the other, it does not matter which",
      "explanation": "**Either** offers a free choice between exactly two things: *either road* means the choice is between two roads and it does not matter which. **Either** followed by **of** plus a pronoun or plural noun (*either of us*, *either of the roads*) belongs to a separate entry.",
      "grammar": {
